<!--
  Static pages only.

  Profile pages are deliberately ABSENT and should stay that way until there is
  a reason to change it. Listing them means either generating this file from the
  database on every deploy (a build step that reaches into production) or serving
  it dynamically from the API (a public, complete, machine-readable list of every
  person on the service — which is precisely the enumeration surface the profile
  endpoint refuses to be). Profiles get found the way they are meant to: somebody
  shares one, and the Pages middleware makes that share unfurl.

  `/claim` is deliberately absent too, for a different reason: it is the same
  page as `/garanta` under an English name, and `marketing-meta.ts` canonicalises
  it to `/garanta`. A sitemap is a list of the URLs we want indexed, so listing a
  URL whose own head disclaims itself asks Google to resolve a contradiction we
  created. It stays reachable, and `robots.txt` still allows it.
-->
